{
  "comment": "Import mapping for The Open Source Drum Kit by Real Music Media, as kept in s1m0n-github/the-open-source-drumkit (its HISE project's Plugin/Samples folder). Every file is one stereo hit at 96 kHz, 24-bit, named by what was hit and numbered quietest to loudest; the importer measures each file's peak to place it in a velocity zone. The snare's 'bottom' and the toms' 'under' sets are separate takes of their own (other lengths and counts), not a second mic of the same hits, so they can't be layered under the top takes and are left out. The hi-hat has no fully open set: half-closed and half-open are its steps between closed and the pedal.",
